{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>The second time</b><br>When the days of the vineyards passed, she returned to her house, and when the trees began to blossom, she said: \"The voice of my beloved\" — and he is like a gazelle in his running, peering through the lattice, perhaps he will see me." "<b>The third time</b><br>And when the end arrived: \"The voice of my beloved.\"" "Behind our wall — in a place where we cannot see." "\"Peering\" — from the windows of the heaven, as in the matter of \"Seeing, I have seen [the affliction of my people].\""], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {2 "The bracketed text [במקום ש] appears to be a gloss supplying 'in a place where'; the closing parenthetical ו(?) after נוכל לראות is unclear, possibly marking an abbreviated word.", 3 "The bracketed phrase [את עני עמי] is supplied from Exodus 3:7, completing the allusion Ibn Ezra cites."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:44:00.957146747Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}